&lt;li&gt;[60m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://app.notion.com/p/sourcegraph/Resources-for-Candidates-Engineering-Interview-Process-c37a70dea5794085bee0c0818c9ef0b3?source=copy_link#3f0a8e11265880d481a4d0e5ac1014d0&quot;&gt;Technical Interview&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎉 Final Interview Stage &lt;/strong&gt;- we move you to our final round, where you gain a better understanding of our business and values holistically…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#e3a04291743048df87541a88aa8199dd&quot;&gt;Values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/How-to-work-with-Quinn-Slack-CEO-807673e0864d473f959cc4efd9642a5a?pvs=4#6f185c0e2011411eac5be9c675f9056c&quot;&gt;Leadership&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We check references and conduct your background check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note - you are welcome to request additional conversations with anyone you would like to meet, but didn’t get to meet during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to bring clarity and control to the world&#39;s most complex codebases. AI is accelerating code creation, but the infrastructure to understand, oversee, and evolve that code hasn&#39;t kept pace. Sourcegraph gives engineering organizations full visibility across their systems, precise context for their agents, and the ability to execute coordinated code changes at scale. As agentic development becomes the dominant engineering paradigm, we provide the context layer teams need to take control of their codebase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Code Search, Deep Search, MCP, and Agentic Batch Changes, we deliver on that mission today - giving engineering teams and their AI tools the cross-repo context to navigate massive codebases with confidence, and the ability to make changes across hundreds of repositories at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Companies like Stripe, Reddit, and Leidos rely on Sourcegraph to ship faster and with higher quality. We&#39;re backed by a16z, Sequoia, and Redpoint, and proud to operate as a globally distributed team that values high agency, direct communication, and customer love.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to build the infrastructure that lets every engineering team - and every agent they deploy - operate on their codebase with confidence, join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hours &amp;amp; location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 While we hire &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/How-we-engage-talent-outside-of-the-US-218f7193695a46cbb1ef39ef9c1f72d4&quot;&gt;almost anywhere&lt;/a&gt; in the world, we have a preference for someone to reside in the following locations for this role. However, if you feel qualified, we welcome you to apply regardless of location. No matter what, working hours must overlap with Pacific Time for at least 25 hours/week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred locations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;USA - West&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this job is exciting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Sr. Product Marketing Manager to help us tell the Sourcegraph story and scale the go-to-market for one of the most critical pieces of engineering infrastructure for the largest enterprises building the future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In this role, you will report to our Head of Marketing, and sit at the intersection of our go-to-market and technical teams to drive thought leadership, product leadership, and market leadership. Our customers are developers and engineering leaders at the largest and most successful companies in the world who rely on us to help them write better code, understand their codebases, secure their products, and adopt the newest and most impactful technology. You will translate deep technical capability into clear market narratives, turn product direction into launches that land, and ensure go-to-market is aligned, credible, and effective.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sourcegraph is a $50m ARR business and growing fast. We are doubling down on our core Search technology, including Deep Search, Code Search, Sourcegraph MCP and APIs for agents, and critical code migration and workflow engines, like Agentic Batch Changes for large-scale changes at scale. You will be responsible for the technical product marketing that will bring that story to life in the market, as well as ensuring alignment with and results from our Demand Gen and DevRel teams.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We move fast and hold ourselves to an extremely high bar for product quality and Developer authenticity. If you’ve made a mark in product marketing for developers, talk to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one month, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ramp up quickly on the product, our audience, and the market landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trust with the GTM and EPD teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify clear product marketing gaps and quick wins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within three months, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clearly defined messaging frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take the lead on product releases and launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and deliver sales enablement assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish strong operating rhythm with GTM and EPD teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within six months, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make product launches and releases repeatable and predictable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high-impact initiatives that directly influence pipe generation and deal velocity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Demand Generation and DevRel on high-impact campaigns&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one year, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly attribute activities to revenue impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape GTM strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the bar for PMM across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have a track record of success in driving and owning product marketing initiatives end-to-end. You’re equally comfortable shaping narratives that connect with our technical enterprise audience, enabling sales, and shipping launches that move the business forward. You understand the software development lifecycle and are excited about how AI is reshaping developer tools and workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of work experience in product marketing, developer marketing, product management, or related technical marketing roles in a B2B enterprise setting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong familiarity with developer tools and modern developer workflows, with a deep interest in AI-driven software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ownership of end-to-end technical product launches, spanning positioning, field enablement, and launch execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to partner closely with technical teams to define what sets Sourcegraph apart and translate that differentiation into clear, credible, and memorable stories across channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise sales motions and navigating complex buying cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sales enablement muscle, building and maintaining high-impact collateral and assets that scale and move enterprise deals forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering integrated campaigns in partnership with Demand Generation, Field Marketing, and DevRel across webinars, videos, web content, and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-first mindset, translating real customer feedback into messaging, positioning, and product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical aptitude, with a deep understanding of how modern software is built, shipped, and adopted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bias toward action, moving quickly and putting bold ideas into motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in software engineering or software development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with account-based marketing (ABM) in enterprise or strategic account motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 This job is an IC4. You can read more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Leveling-Guide-0e1b5c76ada64b9caac387f8b7c4fc66&quot;&gt;our job leveling philosophy&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💸 &lt;/strong&gt;We pay you an above-average salary because we want to hire the best people who are fully focused on helping Sourcegraph succeed, not worried about paying bills. As an &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Mission-values-e9d37e6b972a4ef395c3076aea2bd07d&quot;&gt;open and transparent&lt;/a&gt; company that values &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=4&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt;, our compensation ranges are visible to every single Sourcegraph teammate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your salary is determined by your pay band for the IC4 job level. For determining pay bands, we use a number of market and data-driven salary sources, along with your location zone, and target the high-end of the range to ensure we’re always paying above market regardless of where you live in the world. Both U.S. and international locations are divided into one of four zones, determined by the cost of labor index for each area. The salary for a successful candidate will be based on level, job-related skills, experience, qualifications, and location zone. Please note that the salaries below may be adjusted in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 The target compensation for this role is based on the IC4 pay band for your zone. The start of the IC4 pay band for each zone is listed below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zone 1: $180,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Zone 2: $144,000&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 In addition to our cash compensation, we offer equity (because when we succeed as a company, we want you to succeed, too) and generous &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba&quot;&gt;perks &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Below is the interview process you can expect for this role (you can read more about &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Types-of-interviews-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;the types of interviews&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; in our Handbook). It may look like a lot of steps, but rest assured that we move quickly and the steps are designed to help you get the information needed to determine if we’re the right fit for you… Interviewing is a two-way street, after all!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect the interview process to take 4.75 hours in total.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;👋 Introduction Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we have initial conversations to get to know you better…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#99be5ff628b2414194a0ba79d9f25f13&quot;&gt;Recruiter Screen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#1919882c0cf147c487eb1df40db8a694&quot;&gt;Hiring Manager Screen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧑‍💻 Team Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we then delve into your experience in more depth and introduce you to members of the team, including cross-functional partners…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?source=copy_link#cb00697e95304550a146c32563c0255d&quot;&gt;Cross-functional Collaboration Interview&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[60m]&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Marketing-Interview-Process-7468b9f6f1524c46944ae1a3d883c641?source=copy_link&quot;&gt;Working Session&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#c678a2a86e0e47e4958507e869bf7ded&quot;&gt;Resume Deep Dive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎉 Final Interview Stage &lt;/strong&gt;- we move you to our final round, where you gain a better understanding of our business and values holistically…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#e3a04291743048df87541a88aa8199dd&quot;&gt;Values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[15m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/How-to-work-with-Quinn-Slack-CEO-807673e0864d473f959cc4efd9642a5a?pvs=4#6f185c0e2011411eac5be9c675f9056c&quot;&gt;Leadership&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We check references and conduct your background check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note - you are welcome to request additional conversations with anyone you would like to meet, but didn’t get to meet during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to bring clarity and control to the world&#39;s most complex codebases. AI is accelerating code creation, but the infrastructure to understand, oversee, and evolve that code hasn&#39;t kept pace. Sourcegraph gives engineering organizations full visibility across their systems, precise context for their agents, and the ability to execute coordinated code changes at scale. As agentic development becomes the dominant engineering paradigm, we provide the context layer teams need to take control of their codebase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Code Search, Deep Search, MCP, and Agentic Batch Changes, we deliver on that mission today - giving engineering teams and their AI tools the cross-repo context to navigate massive codebases with confidence, and the ability to make changes across hundreds of repositories at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Companies like Stripe, Reddit, and Leidos rely on Sourcegraph to ship faster and with higher quality. We&#39;re backed by a16z, Sequoia, and Redpoint, and proud to operate as a globally distributed team that values high agency, direct communication, and customer love.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to build the infrastructure that lets every engineering team - and every agent they deploy - operate on their codebase with confidence, join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hours &amp;amp; location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 While we hire &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/How-we-engage-talent-outside-of-the-US-218f7193695a46cbb1ef39ef9c1f72d4&quot;&gt;almost anywhere&lt;/a&gt; in the world, we have a preference for someone to reside in the following locations for this role. However, if you feel qualified, we welcome you to apply regardless of location. No matter what, working hours must overlap with EST for at least 20 hours/week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred locations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this job is exciting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a deeply technical, pragmatic Product Manager to help shape and deliver products for developers and the AI agents working alongside them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will initially be the primary Product Manager supporting a small, fast-moving engineering organization. Rather than being embedded within a single team, you will work across several engineering teams to identify priorities, organize customer and product feedback, define requirements, guide products through the experimental, beta, and general availability lifecycle, and enable our Marketing and Go-To-Market teams to bring it to the world .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will spend significant time working directly with customers, engineering leaders, and developers to understand their needs and translate them into clear product decisions. You will need enough technical depth to discuss implementation tradeoffs, evaluate developer workflows, and represent the product when an engineer is not in the room. You will also need the ability to crisply communicate with non-developers, internal and external, about the value that Sourcegraph delivers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to have an outsized impact within a small organization operating much like a startup, while benefiting from Sourcegraph’s enterprise distribution and access to customers with some of the largest and most complex codebases in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one month, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ramp up on Sourcegraph’s products, customers, technical architecture, go-to-market pitch, and product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong working relationships with engineering leaders and the teams you will support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join customer conversations and develop an understanding of their workflows, pain points, and priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and begin organizing existing customer feedback, product ideas, and active experiments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within three months, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a clear process for gathering, organizing, and prioritizing product feedback across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer problems into clear product requirements, specifications, and success criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help teams make pragmatic prioritization decisions across customer requests, product investments, and technical work including market research and competitive analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the product lifecycle of experimental and beta features, including customer discovery, iteration, launch planning, and measurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide greater clarity beyond engineering on what we are building, why it matters, and how we will determine whether it is successful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within six months, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product prioritization and planning across the engineering teams, and act as the glue between EPD, revenue, and marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide key products from early experimentation through beta and general availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong understanding of Sourcegraph’s customers and become a trusted representative of their needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable systems for product discovery, feedback management, specification, launch, pricing and packaging, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define the broader product strategy for how developers and AI agents make changes across large and complex codebases, and represent that vision in public.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the organization’s ability to make focused, evidence-based product decisions without introducing unnecessary processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Product and Engineering across the company, supporting sales enablement and product marketing functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a deeply technical Product Manager who is comfortable operating across several teams and product areas at once. You can move between customer discovery, strategy, product specifications, prioritization, and launch execution based on what the organization needs most.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are energized by startup environments where roles are broad, context changes quickly, and progress depends on people taking ownership beyond narrowly defined responsibilities. You do not need a large product organization, extensive research support, or a mature operating process to make effective decisions. You are comfortable creating structure where it is useful while avoiding process for its own sake.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are pragmatic. You know that the best product decision is not always the most ambitious or technically sophisticated one. You consider customer value, engineering effort, product quality, strategic importance, and speed when helping teams determine what to build.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have meaningful experience with software development, whether through a previous engineering role or sustained hands-on coding experience. You understand how developers work and can discuss technical constraints and tradeoffs credibly. You can explain and defend product decisions with customers, executives, and engineers, even when the engineering team is not present.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are comfortable spending significant time with customers. You ask thoughtful questions, identify the underlying problems behind feature requests, and distinguish between an individual request and a broader market need. You can turn fragmented feedback into actionable insights and clear product direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are also an excellent communicator. You tell the story behind why a product or initiative matters, creating alignment across engineering and the broader organization. You bring clarity to ambiguous problems without pretending to have certainty where it does not exist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Because this role will work closely with leaders in Eastern Time and with customers primarily located in North America, you must have substantial working-hour overlap with the Eastern Time zone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience working in product management, including experience within an early-stage company, startup, or similarly small and fast-moving organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous professional software engineering experience or substantial hands-on coding experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building technical products for developers, engineering teams, or other highly technical users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with customers throughout product discovery, development, beta testing, and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating customer problems and technical concepts into clear product requirements and specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience prioritizing work across multiple teams, stakeholders, and competing customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate as the primary Product Manager across several engineering teams rather than within one narrowly defined product area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software development workflows, Git, source control, and modern developer tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate credibly with both engineers and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use qualitative feedback, product data, and strategic context to make pragmatic product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively with significant Eastern Time zone overlap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products involving AI agents, coding assistants, code generation, or large language models, and a strong stance on how AI will change the way software is being built.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developer tools, code search, code intelligence, compilers, IDEs, or large-scale code transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise customers and complex software development organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy writing code and are comfortable exploring or contributing to a production codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 This job is an IC4. You can read more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Leveling-Guide-0e1b5c76ada64b9caac387f8b7c4fc66&quot;&gt;our job leveling philosophy&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💸 We pay above-market salaries because we want to hire exceptional people who can focus on building great products, not worrying about paying bills. As an&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Mission-values-e9d37e6b972a4ef395c3076aea2bd07d&quot;&gt; open and transparent&lt;/a&gt; company, our&lt;a href=&quot;https://app.notion.com/p/sourcegraph/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=4&amp;amp;assetsVersion=23.13.20260723.1259&amp;amp;clientBuildTarget=client&quot;&gt; compensation philosophy&lt;/a&gt; and pay bands are visible to every Sourcegraph teammate, and we strive to make our approach equitable, explainable, and competitive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your base salary is determined by the IC4 pay band for your location zone (1-4). Our pay bands are informed by market data and designed to ensure competitive compensation wherever you live. During the recruiting process, we&#39;ll discuss the range applicable to you based on job level, relevant skills, experience, qualifications, and location zone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰The starting salary for the IC4 pay band in each zone is:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zone 2:&lt;/strong&gt; $167,200 USD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zone 3:&lt;/strong&gt; $125,400 USD&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 In addition to competitive cash compensation, we offer meaningful equity (because when Sourcegraph succeeds, we want you to succeed, too) and generous&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba&quot;&gt; perks &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Below is the interview process you can expect for this role (you can read more about &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Types-of-interviews-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;the types of interviews&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; in our Handbook). It may look like a lot of steps, but rest assured that we move quickly and the steps are designed to help you get the information needed to determine if we’re the right fit for you… Interviewing is a two-way street, after all!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect the interview process to take 5.25 hours in total.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;👋 Introduction Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we have initial conversations to get to know you better…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#99be5ff628b2414194a0ba79d9f25f13&quot;&gt;Recruiter Screen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#1919882c0cf147c487eb1df40db8a694&quot;&gt;Hiring Manager Screen&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧑‍💻 Team Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we then delve into your experience in more depth and introduce you to members of the team, including cross-functional partners…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[60m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://app.notion.com/p/sourcegraph/Product-Interview-Process-82297583a0464461b6ee0ce9ec04e76a?source=copy_link#833d70c58d9d4472ace4914549bb5c18&quot;&gt;Async writing project&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://app.notion.com/p/sourcegraph/Product-Interview-Process-82297583a0464461b6ee0ce9ec04e76a?source=copy_link#1d11f8be3fd848f1ae19d54b650fab3e&quot;&gt;Review of proposal&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Product-Interview-Process-82297583a0464461b6ee0ce9ec04e76a#72d47639962b4887894489792fdd64d0&quot;&gt;Product Manager overview of past projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m]&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#c678a2a86e0e47e4958507e869bf7ded&quot;&gt;Resume Deep Dive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎉 Final Interview Stage &lt;/strong&gt;- we move you to our final round, where you gain a better understanding of our business and values holistically…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#e3a04291743048df87541a88aa8199dd&quot;&gt;Values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/How-to-work-with-Quinn-Slack-CEO-807673e0864d473f959cc4efd9642a5a?pvs=4#6f185c0e2011411eac5be9c675f9056c&quot;&gt;Leadership&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We check references and conduct your background check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note - you are welcome to request additional conversations with anyone you would like to meet, but didn’t get to meet during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to bring clarity and control to the world&#39;s most complex codebases. AI is accelerating code creation, but the infrastructure to understand, oversee, and evolve that code hasn&#39;t kept pace. Sourcegraph gives engineering organizations full visibility across their systems, precise context for their agents, and the ability to execute coordinated code changes at scale. As agentic development becomes the dominant engineering paradigm, we provide the context layer teams need to take control of their codebase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Code Search, Deep Search, MCP, and Agentic Batch Changes, we deliver on that mission today - giving engineering teams and their AI tools the cross-repo context to navigate massive codebases with confidence, and the ability to make changes across hundreds of repositories at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Companies like Stripe, Reddit, and Leidos rely on Sourcegraph to ship faster and with higher quality. We&#39;re backed by a16z, Sequoia, and Redpoint, and proud to operate as a globally distributed team that values high agency, direct communication, and customer love.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to build the infrastructure that lets every engineering team - and every agent they deploy - operate on their codebase with confidence, join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hours &amp;amp; location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 While we hire &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/How-we-engage-talent-outside-of-the-US-218f7193695a46cbb1ef39ef9c1f72d4&quot;&gt;almost anywhere&lt;/a&gt; in the world, we have a preference for someone in the United States.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred locations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;United States&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this job is exciting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a small, high-performing Customer Success team at an important point in Sourcegraph&#39;s growth. As a CSM, you&#39;ll manage approximately 40 commercial and enterprise accounts through a scaled model.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll build relationships, drive adoption, identify risk and opportunity, and help customers realize measurable value from Sourcegraph. Across your portfolio, you&#39;ll use customer health, product telemetry, and engagement signals to prioritize where human intervention will have the greatest impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with our Digital Program Manager, who builds and manages the digital programs, content, and automation supporting the scaled segment. This role complements Digital Programs by converting scalable engagement into accountable customer ownership, ensuring customers realize value, risks are proactively managed, and growth opportunities are identified.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role also offers the opportunity to help shape our scaled CS motion by testing engagement strategies, building repeatable plays, and defining how digital and human engagement work together effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one month, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with your CS teammates, Named AEs, Field Engineering counterparts, and Digital Program Manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn our product, value proposition, customers, internal processes, and Customer Success motion, including existing Digital Programs playbooks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand your portfolio, including account history, product adoption, customer health, engagement levels, and renewal timing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shadow customer calls to understand how customers engage with Sourcegraph&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin taking ownership of your accounts and tiering&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish an initial segmentation and coverage approach for your broader portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within three months, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regular customer engagement for your accounts, developing a strong understanding of their workflows, use cases, stakeholders, and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor health, adoption, telemetry, and engagement signals across your portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a coverage strategy across accounts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Digital Program Manager to advance digital programs based on customer insights and engagement data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify accounts requiring deeper engagement, enablement, or risk mitigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently lead standard product trainings and workflow discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Named AEs on customer strategy, renewals, and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute CS plays and experiments that improve adoption, engagement, and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within six months, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage your portfolio, applying the right level of engagement based on customer needs, health, adoption, and opportunity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer and product signals to identify trends, risks, and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build multithreaded relationships and expand adoption across teams, workflows, and use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Digital Program Manager to continuously improve the scaled CS motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish repeatable CS plays and best practices that improve customer engagement and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify clear value narratives across your portfolio of accounts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of the customer internally across Sales, EPD, PMM, and Support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re tech-curious, customer-oriented, and comfortable operating autonomously. You can manage a portfolio of approximately 40 accounts while making thoughtful decisions about where your direct engagement will have the greatest impact and where a scaled motion is more effective.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re comfortable leading a scaled Customer Success motion. You use customer health, product adoption, telemetry, engagement, and business context to prioritize your time and determine the right level of engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re interested in developer tooling and how engineering teams work. You don&#39;t need to be an engineer, but you should be comfortable learning technical products, understanding developer workflows, and leading standard product trainings and workflow discussions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re analytical and commercially minded. You can identify risk, opportunity, and expansion potential from customer and product signals, and connect adoption to meaningful customer outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re a strong partner and collaborator. You can work closely with a Digital Program Manager to turn customer insights into better scaled engagement, while independently owning customer strategy and execution for your accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re proactive, adaptable, and comfortable with ambiguity. You enjoy experimenting, learning from results, and building processes where they don&#39;t yet exist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re curious about AI-assisted development and how it&#39;s changing developer productivity, workflows, and how customers evaluate value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-facing experience in Customer Success, account management, account coordination, technical support, solutions consulting, or a similar role; the title matters less than the experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a large or varied book of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing multiple customers or accounts and making prioritization decisions based on customer needs and business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with digital customer success motion, processes, or workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a technical SaaS environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated comfort presenting to customers or technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in developer tooling, observability, infrastructure, or adjacent technical products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 This job is an IC2.&amp;nbsp; You can read more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Leveling-Guide-0e1b5c76ada64b9caac387f8b7c4fc66&quot;&gt;our job leveling philosophy&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💸 &lt;/strong&gt;We pay you an above-average salary because we want to hire the best people who are fully focused on helping Sourcegraph succeed, not worried about paying bills. As an &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Mission-values-e9d37e6b972a4ef395c3076aea2bd07d&quot;&gt;open and transparent&lt;/a&gt; company that values &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=4&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt;, our compensation ranges are visible to every single Sourcegraph teammate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your salary is determined by your pay band for the IC2 job level. For determining pay bands, we use a number of market and data-driven salary sources, along with your location zone, and target the high-end of the range to ensure we’re always paying above market regardless of where you live in the world. Both U.S. and international locations are divided into one of four zones, determined by the cost of labor index for each area. The salary for a successful candidate will be based on level, job-related skills, experience, qualifications, and location zone. Please note that the salaries below may be adjusted in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 The compensation for this role is $96,640 USD base + $24,160 USD commission for a total OTE of $120,800 USD.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 In addition to our cash compensation, we offer equity (because when we succeed as a company, we want you to succeed, too) and generous&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba&quot;&gt;perks &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Below is the interview process you can expect for this role (you can read more about &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Types-of-interviews-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;the types of interviews&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; in our Handbook). It may look like a lot of steps, but rest assured that we move quickly and the steps are designed to help you get the information needed to determine if we’re the right fit for you… Interviewing is a two-way street, after all!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect the interview process to take 4 hours in total.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;👋 Introduction Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we have initial conversations to get to know you better…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#99be5ff628b2414194a0ba79d9f25f13&quot;&gt;Recruiter Screen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m]&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#1919882c0cf147c487eb1df40db8a694&quot;&gt; Hiring Manager Screen&lt;/a&gt; /&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#c678a2a86e0e47e4958507e869bf7ded&quot;&gt; Resume Deep Dive&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧑‍💻 Team Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we then delve into your experience in more depth and introduce you to members of the team, including cross-functional partners…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[60m]&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#cb00697e95304550a146c32563c0255d&quot;&gt; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#88b9f826dee04ef98afc2aeec35b877a&quot;&gt;Peer&lt;/a&gt; with Digital Program Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[60m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://app.notion.com/p/sourcegraph/Technical-Success-interview-process-902069565e1147b89ac98054179eb676?source=copy_link#9c53f1c6b558427fb131facc9733619f&quot;&gt;Working Session&lt;/a&gt; with Hiring Manager + Named AE + Digital Program Lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎉 Final Interview Stage &lt;/strong&gt;- we move you to our final round, where you gain a better understanding of our business and values holistically…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#e3a04291743048df87541a88aa8199dd&quot;&gt;Values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[15m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/How-to-work-with-Quinn-Slack-CEO-807673e0864d473f959cc4efd9642a5a?pvs=4#6f185c0e2011411eac5be9c675f9056c&quot;&gt;Leadership&lt;/a&gt; with CRO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We check references and conduct your background check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note - you are welcome to request additional conversations with anyone you would like to meet, but didn’t get to meet during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to bring clarity and control to the world&#39;s most complex codebases. AI is accelerating code creation, but the infrastructure to understand, oversee, and evolve that code hasn&#39;t kept pace. Sourcegraph gives engineering organizations full visibility across their systems, precise context for their agents, and the ability to execute coordinated code changes at scale. As agentic development becomes the dominant engineering paradigm, we provide the context layer teams need to take control of their codebase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Code Search, Deep Search, MCP, and Agentic Batch Changes, we deliver on that mission today - giving engineering teams and their AI tools the cross-repo context to navigate massive codebases with confidence, and the ability to make changes across hundreds of repositories at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Companies like Stripe, Reddit, and Leidos rely on Sourcegraph to ship faster and with higher quality. We&#39;re backed by a16z, Sequoia, and Redpoint, and proud to operate as a globally distributed team that values high agency, direct communication, and customer love.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to build the infrastructure that lets every engineering team - and every agent they deploy - operate on their codebase with confidence, join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hours &amp;amp; location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required working locations, one of:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Austin, TX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chicago, IL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Denver, CO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seattle, WA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this job is exciting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph gives engineering teams complete context to understand, oversee, and evolve large, complex codebases. As agent adoption grows across enterprise engineering, the need for that context is only becoming more critical. Some of the largest engineering organizations in the world already rely on us for it, but we need to tell this story more broadly. That&#39;s where you come in: you&#39;ll rebuild our outbound motion by prospecting yourself first, while concurrently managing our outsourced SDR team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one month, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete your onboarding, going deep into our ICP, product, customer wins and losses, and recent and current pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn our value framework and messaging house both of which will be critical to your personal success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take over day-to-day management of our outsourced third-party SDR team: understand their current motion, targets, and output, and where the gaps are&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Revamp our cold-call and LinkedIn messaging scripts, and start personally testing new messaging in-market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📅 Within one quarter, you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a consistent outbound motion yourself — cold calls + LinkedIn — generating qualified net-new pipeline against a personal target&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tighten the outsourced team: QA their messaging, coach, and hold them to activity and pipeline goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn what&#39;s working into a documented, repeatable outbound playbook — proven by your own results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and hit net-new outbound pipeline goals across both your direct effort and the outsourced team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅&lt;/strong&gt; Beyond one quarter (if the above is working), you will…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and lead an in-house SDR team, scaling the playbook you&#39;ve validated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own onboarding, coaching cadence, and pipeline targets for that team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a foundational role for our business. You&#39;ll re-introduce the outbound prospecting motion at Sourcegraph and prove it out yourself before scaling it into a team. You&#39;re a hunter first: you love the cold call, the LinkedIn thread, and the challenge of getting a busy engineering leader to pay attention. But you also think like a builder and a coach;&amp;nbsp; you&#39;ll manage our outsourced SDR team from day one, sharpen the scripts and cadences, and turn what&#39;s working into a playbook others can run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your skill-set:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years in outbound sales development / prospecting, with a track record of personally generating net-new enterprise pipeline via cold calling, email, and social&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Player-coach mentality you&#39;ll pick up the phone and prospect directly, not just manage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0 → 1 builder: you&#39;ve created scripts, cadences, and playbooks from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb written and verbal communication; you can craft and A/B test messaging that converts skeptics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to sell into technical/engineering audiences and ramp on a technical product quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency, gritty, comfortable with ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven: you measure and iterate on activity → meeting → pipeline conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in developer tools or an adjacent technical domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or coaching reps, or an outsourced/agency SDR team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Level&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 This job is an IC4.&amp;nbsp; You can read more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Leveling-Guide-0e1b5c76ada64b9caac387f8b7c4fc66&quot;&gt;our job leveling philosophy&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;💸 &lt;/strong&gt;We pay you an above-average salary because we want to hire the best people who are fully focused on helping Sourcegraph succeed, not worried about paying bills. As an &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Mission-values-e9d37e6b972a4ef395c3076aea2bd07d&quot;&gt;open and transparent&lt;/a&gt; company that values &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=4&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt;, our compensation ranges are visible to every single Sourcegraph teammate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your salary is determined by your pay band for the IC4&amp;nbsp; job level. For determining pay bands, we use a number of market and data-driven salary sources, along with your location zone, and target the high-end of the range to ensure we’re always paying above market regardless of where you live in the world. Both U.S. and international locations are divided into one of four zones, determined by the cost of labor index for each area. The salary for a successful candidate will be based on level, job-related skills, experience, qualifications, and location zone. Please note that the salaries below may be adjusted in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 The compensation for this role is $119,000 USD base + $51,000 USD variable ($170,000 USD on-target-earnings).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 In addition to our cash compensation, we offer equity (because when we succeed as a company, we want you to succeed, too) and generous &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba&quot;&gt;perks &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interview process&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Below is the interview process you can expect for this role (you can read more about &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Types-of-interviews-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;the types of interviews&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; in our Handbook). It may look like a lot of steps, but rest assured that we move quickly and the steps are designed to help you get the information needed to determine if we’re the right fit for you… Interviewing is a two-way street, after all!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect the interview process to take 3.25 hours in total.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;👋 Introduction Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we have initial conversations to get to know you better…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#99be5ff628b2414194a0ba79d9f25f13&quot;&gt;Recruiter Screen&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#1919882c0cf147c487eb1df40db8a694&quot;&gt;Hiring Manager Screen&lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#c678a2a86e0e47e4958507e869bf7ded&quot;&gt;Resume Deep Dive&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🧑‍💻 Team Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we then delve into your experience in more depth and introduce you to members of the team, including cross-functional partners…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#cb00697e95304550a146c32563c0255d&quot;&gt;Cross-functional team collaboration&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🎉 Final Interview Stage &lt;/strong&gt;- we move you to our final round, where you gain a better understanding of our business and values holistically…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30m] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#e3a04291743048df87541a88aa8199dd&quot;&gt;Values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[60m] Working session&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We check references and conduct your background check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note - you are welcome to request additional conversations with anyone you would like to meet, but didn’t get to meet during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to bring clarity and control to the world&#39;s most complex codebases. AI is accelerating code creation, but the infrastructure to understand, oversee, and evolve that code hasn&#39;t kept pace. Sourcegraph gives engineering organizations full visibility across their systems, precise context for their agents, and the ability to execute coordinated code changes at scale. As agentic development becomes the dominant engineering paradigm, we provide the context layer teams need to take control of their codebase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Code Search, Deep Search, MCP, and Agentic Batch Changes, we deliver on that mission today - giving engineering teams and their AI tools the cross-repo context to navigate massive codebases with confidence, and the ability to make changes across hundreds of repositories at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Companies like Stripe, Reddit, and Leidos rely on Sourcegraph to ship faster and with higher quality. We&#39;re backed by a16z, Sequoia, and Redpoint, and proud to operate as a globally distributed team that values high agency, direct communication, and customer love.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to build the infrastructure that lets every engineering team - and every agent they deploy - operate on their codebase with confidence, join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Working hours&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 While we are an all-remote company and hire&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/How-we-engage-talent-outside-of-the-US-218f7193695a46cbb1ef39ef9c1f72d4&quot;&gt; almost anywhere&lt;/a&gt; in the world, we do require successful candidates to be located in the United States.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred location:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;USA&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Why this job is exciting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Account Executive [IC5], you will have more responsibility, upside, and growth potential than anywhere else with a comparable role. At Sourcegraph, we strive to create the best environment for exceptionally talented people to thrive. If you join us, you’ll make a meaningful impact on how engineering organizations operate at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s what you can expect in your first year:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within one month, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin 1:1’s with your manager, understand your 30-60-90 plan, shadow current team members, review your quota, and dive into your territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a territory plan targeting net-new logo accounts with a strong emphasis on outbound engagement and expanding existing customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start to hold new business meetings and build pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet key partners across Customer Engineering, Technical Success, Product, Legal, and Engineering teams—relationships that will be critical throughout your deal cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within three months, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be well versed in Sourcegraph’s Value Framework.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the unique capabilities of Sourcegraph products and develop compelling strategies to align their value with your prospect’s engineering and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hone your storytelling skills, clearly articulating use cases, sharing real-world customer success stories, and conveying outcomes that matter to both technical and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify champions, influencers, and decision makers, building trusted advisor relationships that accelerate adoption across engineering organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute a disciplined, repeatable sales process to continuously build and advance pipeline while maintaining accurate forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate complex enterprise proposals and contracts and surface market insights to the Product team to influence our roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently hit your activity and pipeline goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within six months, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, consistently meeting and exceeding pipeline and revenue objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Customer Engineering, Product, Legal, and Engineering to successfully close technically complex and strategically significant enterprise deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver actionable customer feedback across teams, ensuring engineers and product teams remain tightly aligned with customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within one year, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be recognized as a top-performing Account Executive, consistently exceeding goals and setting the standard for excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support new Account Executives, assisting with onboarding, training, and motivation to elevate the entire team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a results-oriented, strategic hunter who thrives in enterprise environments and has a proven track record selling to developers and engineering leaders. You excel at uncovering needs through rigorous discovery, navigating complex multi-stakeholder deals, and building consensus across technical and executive audiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are highly motivated, self-directed, and energized by creating new opportunities and expanding your footprint within accounts. You take ownership of your pipeline and performance, and you hold yourself accountable for achieving ambitious goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of B2B SaaS or software sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of selling as an Enterprise Account Executive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of exceeding quotas while leading with empathy and credibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling complex solutions with ASP ≥ $100k&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable engaging with both individual contributors and VP/C-level executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional interpersonal, presentation, verbal, and written communication skills across all levels and personas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for our mission and belief in the transformative power of developer productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling developer or engineering-focused products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software development concepts, CI/CD, version control, or DevOps tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex multi-year contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of security, licensing, and compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vertical expertise in Financial Services, Insurance, Semiconductors, Auto-Manufacturing, or Retail.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 This job is an IC5. You can read more about&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Leveling-Guide-0e1b5c76ada64b9caac387f8b7c4fc66?pvs=4&quot;&gt;our job leveling philosophy&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Compensation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💸 We pay you an above-average salary because we want to hire the best people who are fully focused on helping Sourcegraph succeed, not worried about paying bills. As an &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Mission-values-e9d37e6b972a4ef395c3076aea2bd07d&quot;&gt;open and transparent&lt;/a&gt; company that values &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt;, our compensation ranges are visible to every single Sourcegraph teammate.&amp;nbsp;To determine your salary, we use a number of market and data-driven salary sources, along with your location zone, and target the high-end of the range to ensure we’re always paying above market regardless of where you live in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰The compensation for this role is outlined below:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IC5: $165,000 USD base + $165,000 USD variable ($330,000 USD on-target-earnings).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 In addition to our cash compensation, we offer equity (because when we succeed as a company, we want you to succeed, too) and generous &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba&quot;&gt;perks &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Interview process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below is the interview process you can expect for this role (you can read more about&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Types-of-interviews-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7&quot;&gt; the types of interviews&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook). It may look like a lot of steps, but rest assured that we move quickly and the steps are designed to help you get the information needed to determine if we’re the right fit for you… Interviewing is a two-way street, after all!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect the interview process to take 5 hours in total.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👋 &lt;strong&gt;Introduction Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we have initial conversations to get to know you better…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min]&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#99be5ff628b2414194a0ba79d9f25f13&quot;&gt; Recruiter Screen&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#1919882c0cf147c487eb1df40db8a694&quot;&gt;Hiring Manager screen&lt;/a&gt; with Regional Sales Director&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[60 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#c678a2a86e0e47e4958507e869bf7ded&quot;&gt;Resume Deep Dive&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧑‍💻 &lt;strong&gt;Team Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we then delve into your experience in more depth and introduce you to members of the team, including cross-functional partners…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#88b9f826dee04ef98afc2aeec35b877a&quot;&gt;Peer&lt;/a&gt; with an Account Executive &amp;amp; Solutions Engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Sales-Interview-Process-3e8dd4fe14d845ffb44e2618f303365f?pvs=4#3eaf05ce8bb44b3584a14dd4c2d03fe9&quot;&gt;Sales Presentation&lt;/a&gt; with RSD, Global Head of Sales, CRO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#e3a04291743048df87541a88aa8199dd&quot;&gt;Values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;strong&gt;Final Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we move you to our final round, where you gain a better understanding of our business and values holistically&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min]&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7#80e2ecaed5854b1ba510b2e391c0c67b&quot;&gt; Leadership&lt;/a&gt; with Global Head of Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We check references and conduct your background check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note - you are welcome to request additional conversations with anyone you would like to meet, but didn’t get to meet during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to bring clarity and control to the world&#39;s most complex codebases. AI is accelerating code creation, but the infrastructure to understand, oversee, and evolve that code hasn&#39;t kept pace. Sourcegraph gives engineering organizations full visibility across their systems, precise context for their agents, and the ability to execute coordinated code changes at scale. As agentic development becomes the dominant engineering paradigm, we provide the context layer teams need to take control of their codebase.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With Code Search, Deep Search, MCP, and Agentic Batch Changes, we deliver on that mission today - giving engineering teams and their AI tools the cross-repo context to navigate massive codebases with confidence, and the ability to make changes across hundreds of repositories at once.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Companies like Stripe, Reddit, and Leidos rely on Sourcegraph to ship faster and with higher quality. We&#39;re backed by a16z, Sequoia, and Redpoint, and proud to operate as a globally distributed team that values high agency, direct communication, and customer love.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you want to build the infrastructure that lets every engineering team - and every agent they deploy - operate on their codebase with confidence, join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Working hours&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 While we are an all-remote company and hire&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/How-we-engage-talent-outside-of-the-US-218f7193695a46cbb1ef39ef9c1f72d4&quot;&gt; almost anywhere&lt;/a&gt; in the world, we do require successful candidates to be located in the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred location:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;USA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Why this job is exciting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Commercial Account Executive, you will have more responsibility, upside, and growth potential than anywhere else otherwise comparable. We strive to make Sourcegraph the best company where exceptionally talented people can thrive. If you join us, we know you’ll make a big impact!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s what you can expect in your first year:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within one month, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Begin 1:1’s with your manager, understand your 30-60-90 plan, meet &amp;amp; shadow current members of the Sourcegraph team, understand your quota, and delve into your territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set your OKRs (Objectives and Key Results) with your manager and develop an action plan to achieve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start to hold new business meetings and build pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet key partners in Customer Engineering, Product, Legal and Engineering teams - they will be key relationships for you throughout your deal cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within three months, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be well versed in Sourcegraph’s Value Framework.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the unique capabilities of Sourcegraph&amp;nbsp; products and develop compelling strategies to align their value with your prospect’s engineering and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hone your storytelling skills, clearly articulating use cases, sharing real-world customer success stories, and conveying outcomes that matter to both technical and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify champions, influencers, and decision makers, building trusted advisor relationships that accelerate adoption across engineering organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute a disciplined, repeatable sales process to continuously build and advance pipeline while maintaining accurate forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate value based proposals and contracts and surface market insights to the Product team to influence our roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently hit your activity and pipeline goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within six months, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, consistently meeting and exceeding pipeline and revenue objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Customer Engineering, Product, Legal, and Engineering to successfully close technically complex and strategically significant enterprise deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver actionable customer feedback across teams, ensuring engineers and product teams remain tightly aligned with customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;📅 Within one year, you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be considered a top-performing Account Executive on the team by consistently exceeding your goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set an example for new Account Executives, and assist in training, onboarding and motivating new Teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;About you&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a results-oriented, motivated, and strategic ‘hunter’ who shares our values and has a passion for all things sales and is laser-focused on generating new greenfield business. Specifically, you will play a pivotal role in helping us achieve our goals by winning high visibility deals and crushing your annual quota.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Skills and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of B2B SaaS or software sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of exceeding sales quotas, while leading with empathy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling complex products with ACV &amp;gt;=&amp;nbsp; $30k&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stellar interpersonal, presentation, verbal, and written communication skills, across all levels and personas (be it with a developer, a CTO, another salesperson, or anyone in-between)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiastic about our mission and the potential for developers to improve the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling developer or engineering-focused products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software development concepts, CI/CD, version control, or DevOps tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex multi-year contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of security, licensing, and compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Level&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📊 This job is an IC2. You can read more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Leveling-Guide-0e1b5c76ada64b9caac387f8b7c4fc66?pvs=4&quot;&gt;our job leveling philosophy&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Compensation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💸 We pay you an above-average salary because we want to hire the best people who are fully focused on helping Sourcegraph succeed, not worried about paying bills. As an&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Mission-values-e9d37e6b972a4ef395c3076aea2bd07d&quot;&gt; open and transparent&lt;/a&gt; company that values&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d&quot;&gt; competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt;, our compensation ranges are visible to every single Sourcegraph teammate. To determine your salary, we use a number of market and data-driven salary sources, along with your location zone, and target the high-end of the range to ensure we’re always paying above market regardless of where you live in the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰The compensation for this role is $91,500 USD base + $91,500 variable ($183,000 USD on-target-earnings).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;📈 In addition to our cash compensation, we offer equity (because when we succeed as a company, we want you to succeed, too) and generous&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba&quot;&gt; perks &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Interview process&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Below is the interview process you can expect for this role (you can read more about&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Types-of-interviews-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7&quot;&gt; the types of interviews&lt;/a&gt; in our Handbook). It may look like a lot of steps, but rest assured that we move quickly and the steps are designed to help you get the information needed to determine if we’re the right fit for you… interviewing is a two-way street, after all!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect the interview process to take 4.5 hours in total.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👋 &lt;strong&gt;Introduction Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we have initial conversations to get to know you better…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min]&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#99be5ff628b2414194a0ba79d9f25f13&quot;&gt; Recruiter Screen&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#1919882c0cf147c487eb1df40db8a694&quot;&gt;Hiring Manager screen&lt;/a&gt; with Regional Sales Director&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[60 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#c678a2a86e0e47e4958507e869bf7ded&quot;&gt;Resume Deep Dive&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧑‍💻 &lt;strong&gt;Team Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we then delve into your experience in more depth and introduce you to members of the team, including cross-functional partners…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#88b9f826dee04ef98afc2aeec35b877a&quot;&gt;Peer&lt;/a&gt; with an Account Executive &amp;amp; Customer Engineer or CSM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[45 min] Sales Presentation with RSD, Head of Global Sales, CRO&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min] &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7?pvs=4#e3a04291743048df87541a88aa8199dd&quot;&gt;Values&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎉 &lt;strong&gt;Final Interview Stage&lt;/strong&gt; - we move you to our final round, where you gain a better understanding of our business and values holistically&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;[30 min]&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/sourcegraph/Types-of-interviews-sample-questions-f279f080583d49ee9f2c60e30c8cb1f7#80e2ecaed5854b1ba510b2e391c0c67b&quot;&gt; Leadership&lt;/a&gt; with Global Head of Sales&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We check references and conduct your background check&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note - you are welcome to request additional conversations with anyone you would like to meet, but didn’t get to meet during the interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(243, 78, 63);&quot;&gt;Learn more about us&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can learn more about what it is like to work at Sourcegraph by reading &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/d7614e3e9dc04c09ac2d42d57f1816e6?v=2a6d426dbae14390b155120b0c029ce0&quot;&gt;our handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an ambitious team who are collectively working hard to build the most influential company in the world. You can read more about our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/What-it-s-like-working-at-Sourcegraph-119a8e11265880b18911eee4d9b7c460#119a8e1126588062b935fc66104b6115&quot;&gt;culture&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Compensation-Pay-Transparency-at-Sourcegraph-d58d0774f51b4b489d41c3628d30ff8d?pvs=74&quot;&gt;competitive compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/Benefits-Perks-dd1da4b6b3a64780abed010a144d34ba?pvs=74&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt; here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sourcegraph is an equal opportunity workplace; we welcome people from all backgrounds.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sourcegraph participates in &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sourcegraph.notion.site/E-Verify-2ab3286dde3446d6bac2898c83610107&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt; for U.S. Employees. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Principal Product Manager, Software Factory, you’ll define and bring together GitLab’s end-to-end software creation experience, from planning and specification through coding, review, and verification. You’ll connect capabilities across GitLab Duo Agent Platform and the wider GitLab product so customers have a cohesive and delightful experience. This is a senior, high-visibility role for a product leader who can shape product direction, work across organizational boundaries, and clearly present recommendations to executive leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the product vision and strategy for GitLab’s end-to-end software factory experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring together planning, specification, coding, review, and verification workflows into a cohesive product experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, engineering, design, and go-to-market teams across GitLab to align priorities and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps, dependencies, and opportunities across GitLab Duo Agent Platform and related areas of the GitLab product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use strong product and design judgment to make complex workflows clear and useful for customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build support for product decisions through clear communication, negotiation, and cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present product direction, tradeoffs, and recommendations to senior and executive leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape how GitLab brings its software factory vision to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management experience at principal scope, leading complex products or experiences across multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of the end-to-end software development workflow, from planning through verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with artificial intelligence products, developer tools, DevSecOps platforms, or related technical products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical judgment that supports effective collaboration with engineering teams and informed product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product design and user experience instincts, including the ability to connect separate capabilities into a coherent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing across functions, resolving competing priorities, and moving work forward without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication and presentation skills, including experience working with senior and executive leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset and the ability to make progress in a fast-changing product area with some ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome candidates with different backgrounds and transferable experience. If this role excites you, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every qualification.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will work across GitLab to connect the teams building the future of our AI-powered DevSecOps platform. You’ll partner closely with the GitLab Duo Agent Platform organization and with product areas that own key parts of the software development workflow. The team’s central challenge is to turn work delivered across several groups into one clear, end-to-end experience for customers while supporting GitLab’s mission to enable everyone to contribute to and co-create the software that powers our world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
