&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h4&gt;Why Kimchi?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Great models are raw ingredients. Kimchi is what happens when you ferment them with good&amp;nbsp;engineering. We started inside CAST AI helping companies run LLMs on their own Kubernetes&amp;nbsp;clusters; today we run our own coding harness on any LLM you pick.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Kimchi Studio&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Studio is where your team&#39;s agents work together: a desktop app that brings autonomous coding&amp;nbsp;agents, model orchestration, and your entire toolchain into one collaborative UI. Multiple agents on&amp;nbsp;separate branches side by side with native git worktree support. Every agent action visible, diffable,&lt;br&gt;and undoable. Local first on your machine, remote sessions when you need them.&lt;br&gt;You&#39;ll own features end to end: design, implementation, testing, production rollout. Most projects&amp;nbsp;ship in 1-4 weeks. You&#39;ll work directly with product and other engineering teams on problems that&amp;nbsp;don&#39;t have textbook solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;You might be a fit if…&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve personally driven a complex product feature from idea to shipped, and you can tell that&amp;nbsp;story with receipts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re a full-stack engineer: TypeScript where the product lives (Electron/React UI, Node&amp;nbsp;services) and Go where the backend lives. Strong in one, ready to go deep in the other, and&amp;nbsp;honest about which is which.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have deep debugging and performance instincts: when the app janks or a query slows down,&amp;nbsp;you find the cause through query profiles and flame graphs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You care about UX, speed, and polish. In a desktop app every millisecond is visible, and you push&amp;nbsp;back when something feels wrong.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus:&lt;/strong&gt; shipping Electron apps at scale (updates, code signing, multi-platform builds), Kubernetes&amp;nbsp;internals, or building your own AI workflows and harnesses at home.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What’s in it for you?&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary (€6,500 - €9,000 gross, depending on the level of experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy a flexible, remote-first global environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a global team of cloud experts and innovators, passionate about pushing the boundaries of Kubernetes technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equity options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get quick feedback with a fast-paced workflow. Most feature projects are completed in 1 to 4 weeks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend 10% of your work time on personal projects or self-improvement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning budget for professional and personal development - including access to international conferences and courses that elevate your skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual hackathon to spark new ideas and strengthen team bonds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team-building budget and company events to connect with your colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equipment budget to ensure you have everything you need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extra days off to help maintain a healthy work-life balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
